course: dictionary
lesson: 11769
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Barrow is one of them. The other words in the sentence are clues that show you which meaning fits. «Sam pushed the barrow full of soil to the vegetable patch.» Pushed, soil and patch are the clues. A barrow here is a wheelbarrow, a cart for carrying soil in the garden.
explain: «Mia's dad sold apples from a barrow in the market.» Sold and market are the clues. This barrow is a small two-wheeled cart used by a street seller. «The walkers climbed the grassy barrow to look at the view.» Climbed and grassy tell you this is a mound of earth, not a cart.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it. If the sentence still makes sense with the meaning you chose, you are probably right.
fact: A barrow can be a wheelbarrow: a small cart with one wheel at the front and two handles, pushed by hand.
fact: In the UK, a barrow can be a small cart with two wheels, used by street sellers to sell fruit and other goods.
fact: In history, a barrow is a large mound of earth built long ago over a grave.
fact: Long barrows and round barrows are ancient burial mounds from the Stone Age and Bronze Age.
fact: A barrow boy is a street trader.
exercise: «Sam pushed the barrow full of soil to the vegetable patch.» What is the barrow? | A bird that sings in the garden | *A wheelbarrow for carrying soil | A grave from long ago | A type of bread
exercise: «Mia's dad sold apples from a barrow in the market.» What kind of barrow is this? | A tall tower of bricks | A school desk | A large mound of earth built long ago | *A small two-wheeled cart used by a street seller
exercise: «The walkers climbed the grassy barrow to look at the view.» What is a barrow here? | A bridge over a stream | A wheelbarrow full of soil | A market cart | *A large mound of earth built long ago over a grave
test: «Builders filled the barrow with bricks and carried them to the wall.» What is the barrow? | A mound of earth over a grave | *A wheelbarrow | A bird's nest | A market stall
test: Ella asks, «What is a barrow boy?» What is the answer? | A boy who works in a garden | A boy who lives in a burial mound | *A street trader | A boy who builds walls
exam: «The Stone Age barrow stood on the empty hill.» What does barrow mean here? | A small two-wheeled cart for selling fruit | *A large mound of earth built long ago over a grave | A cart with one wheel and two handles | A garden tool for weeding
